    thinking: "**Analyzing Hero Layout Design**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the Hero layout, specifically aligning it with the provided dark-themed image. The navigation is prioritized at the top, following the image structure, with the title on the left and a menu on the right within a pill shape. The black background and person\'s photo will be added to the layout. The main text content will be placed to the right side of the image.\n\n\n**Restructuring Hero and Navigation**\n\nI\'ve been examining the current `Hero.tsx` component and realizing the image and text order needs swapping, which I\'ll implement by switching their order. The title and menu placement are also noted; it appears the title should act as a header in the top left, and the menu should be on the right, as seen in the image. I\'ll restructure both `Navigation.tsx` and `Hero.tsx` to reflect this new layout.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation and Hero**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the navigation bar, deciding on its final look and feel based on the reference image. I\'ll need to update `Navigation.tsx` to match the visual style of the screenshot. I will include the doctor\'s name and profession on the left side, and a rounded, dark menu on the right. This requires careful adjustment of the title, which will now incorporate a subtitle to match the visual language. I\'ll also update the Hero component accordingly.\n\n\n**Implementing New Navigation Layout**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new navigation bar, incorporating the doctor\'s name and profession on the left and a pill-shaped menu on the right, as specified. I\'m focusing on the font styles for the doctor\'s name, which I\'m setting as a large serif font, and the profession, a smaller sans-serif in gray. I\'ve also begun to rewrite the `Hero.tsx` to align the image and text content, modifying the header and content per the new mock. I\'m swapping the image to the left and will include only the introductory text in the body.\n\n\n**Adjusting Navigation Layout**\n\nI\'m now implementing the navigation structure based on the screenshot, which shows a single-line navigation on desktop. The text will be white on a black background, in a similar fashion to the header. I\'m focusing on making sure to switch to the new style for a responsive design with the pill-shaped menu. I need to make sure the header is responsive and adjusts properly for mobile.\n\n\n**Optimizing Navigation for Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m working on making the navigation responsive, prioritizing a good desktop experience. I\'m focusing on flex-wrapping or scrolling for the mobile view, and have started refining `Navigation.tsx`. The current focus is ensuring the desktop and mobile navigation styles function seamlessly. I\'m looking to optimize the mobile view to make sure it looks great.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation Implementation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the mobile navigation toggle and menu, using `AnimatePresence` for smooth transitions. The menu appears upon toggle click, featuring links formatted for mobile screens, and hides on click. The mobile menu background is black and includes the doctor\'s name, mirroring the desktop header. I\'m focusing on ensuring responsiveness with the menu.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Hero and Navigation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the mobile navigation toggle and menu. The black background includes the doctor\'s name, mirroring the desktop header. I\'m finalizing the Hero section, ensuring the bust image and introductory text integrate with the layout. The goal is to achieve visual cohesion.\n\n\n**Integrating Image and Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the image into the hero section, placing it on the left on desktop. I\'m focusing on the responsive design, using `grid` and `motion.div` to ensure the image displays correctly on all devices. I\'ve added a gradient overlay to enhance the image contrast and blend it seamlessly with the black background. The image is set to be grayscale and high contrast.\n\n\n**Enhancing Hero Text Placement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing text placement within the Hero section, particularly on mobile. I\'m leveraging the introductory paragraph and incorporating elements like \"Hola, soy el Dr. Samuel Silva\" to ensure it\'s easy to read across devices. I\'m also addressing text wrapping on smaller screens, using flexbox or grid. I\'ll test it out and look into responsive adjustments.\n\n\n**Refining Hero Content Display**\n\nI\'m now refining the Hero section\'s content to match the screenshot precisely. I\'m removing the \"Conoce m\303\241s\" button entirely. I\'ll focus on ensuring the primary text, including the introductory paragraph, is displayed with correct styling, particularly its size and responsiveness. I\'ve re-reviewed the screenshot and will make it more compact.\n\n\n**Implementing Text-Based Hero**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Hero section layout as requested, focusing on the text-only format from the image. I\'m removing the CTA button and adjusting the `Navigation.tsx` to match the new image. I\'ll be working in the Hero to match the provided layout.\n\n\n**Developing Navigation Styling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the desktop navigation styling, specifically the text links. I\'m prioritizing the visual cohesion, aligning text size, font, and colors with the provided screenshot. The goal is to make the navigation elements match the design language. I\'m also now adjusting the mobile navigation toggle and menu to ensure a seamless experience.\n\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Navigation Menu**\n\nI\'m now refining the mobile navigation menu\'s visual appearance and responsiveness, using a black background with Dr. Silva\'s name and profession at the top, a clear close button, and larger sans-serif font for the menu items. I\'m focusing on ensuring smooth transitions with `AnimatePresence`. I\'m going to also work on making sure everything fits the mobile display.\n\n\n\n**Adjusting Hero Image Layout**\n\nI\'m now integrating the image into the hero section on the left, implementing a subtle gradient overlay to enhance its appearance against the black background. I\'m focusing on the image responsiveness using `grid` and `motion.div` ensuring it\'s optimal on all devices.\n\n\n**Optimizing Hero Content Styling**\n\nI\'m now integrating the image into the hero section and focusing on the accompanying text\'s layout, ensuring it\'s optimally placed alongside the image. I\'ve re-reviewed the layout and will be ensuring the `Hola, soy...` paragraph is easily readable across all devices. I\'m focusing on ensuring visual coherence. I\'ve been adjusting the gradient over the image.\n\n\n**Refining Hero Image Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the hero image, determining the best `object-fit` and layout for a rectangle photo. After reviewing, I\'ve decided to use `object-cover` with a black background to best blend the gradient overlay. I\'ll test how it looks with the `bg-gradient-to-r` on the right side of the image, and then remove it to make sure it looks great. I\'ll also try a bottom gradient.\n\n\n"
